dialect protocol
protocol stdio.zip.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.zip
start op
framing record

# P2-P2: `ZipMutation::encode_op`/`decode_op` (../🦀️component.rs's `OpCodecs` region) were ALREADY
# real binary before this wave — a pure forward to `dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`/`decode_op`
# (`🧰️framework/…/🗣️dsl/🦀️component.rs`'s `#region OpRt`), the generic layout every `DslVariants`
# type shares: `format u8` (=1, `store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT`) + `ordinal varint` (the
# `ZipMutation` variant's position in `DslVariants::variants()`, in the SAME declaration order as
# this facet's own `../📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio`'s `op` alternatives) + a
# `pack_rt::encode_record_body`-produced record body. `format`/`ordinal` are real, protocol-
# walkable fixed-shape fields; the record body's own field layout genuinely depends on WHICH
# variant `ordinal` selects (13 different shapes, one per `ZipMutation` variant) — no single
# `field`/`segment` list in this dialect can describe all 13 at once without a tag-dispatched
# `repeat` whose arms embed a full nested `RecordSpec` walk, which this dialect does not have (the
# `Prim::Ref` recursion this would need is the same unresolved gap the P2-P1 json pilot already
# filed as a `mechanism_gaps` entry). Modeled honestly: the two real fixed fields, then one opaque
# trailing `chain ... bytes` for the per-variant body — the Rust encode/decode side (via
# `pack_rt::encode_record_body`/`decode_record_body`) IS genuinely spec-driven structured binary,
# just not walkable field-by-field at THIS declarative layer.

field format u8
field ordinal varint
chain payload bytes
